    "dc.description.abstract" : [ {
      "value" : "Summary of the Sexual Harassment of Women at Workplace (Prevention, Prohibition and Redressal) Act, 2013\nKey Provisions\nDefinitions\n•\tAggrieved Woman: A woman subjected to sexual harassment.\n•\tSexual Harassment: Unwelcome sexual conduct (physical, verbal, or non-verbal).\n•\tWorkplace: Includes all work environments, public or private, and dwelling places for domestic workers.\nRedressal Mechanisms\n1.\tInternal Complaints Committee (ICC): Mandatory for employers with 10+ employees.\n2.\tLocal Complaints Committee (LCC): For areas without ICCs, led by the District Officer.\nComplaint and Inquiry Process\n•\tFiling: Within 3 months (extendable by 3 months under certain conditions).\n•\tConciliation: Optional, non-monetary, at the aggrieved woman’s request.\n•\tInquiry:\n•\tConducted by ICC/LCC with civil court-like powers.\n•\tCompletion within 90 days.\nActions and Penalties\n•\tProven Allegation:\n•\tAction against the respondent per service rules.\n•\tSalary deduction for the aggrieved woman’s compensation.\n•\tFalse/Malicious Allegation:\n•\tAction against the complainant per service rules.\n•\tEmployer Non-Compliance:\n•\tFine up to ₹50,000.\n•\tRepeat offences may lead to license cancellation.\nEmployer Responsibilities\n•\tEnsure a safe working environment.\n•\tDisplay ICC details and penalties.\n•\tOrganize awareness programs.\n•\tAssist in inquiries and implement recommendations.\nMiscellaneous Provisions\n•\tAnnual Reports: To employer and District Officer.\n•\tMonitoring and Data: By the appropriate Government.\n•\tPublicity: By the appropriate Government.\n•\tPenalty for Unauthorized Publication: Of complaint details.\n•\tAppeal: Within 90 days, as per service rules or prescribed.",
      "language" : null,
      "authority" : null,
      "confidence" : -1,
      "place" : 0
    } ],
